+## 2026-10-11 — the 120 Hz mode measured until it settles, and kept under VRR (PS5 Mesa 08ba193)
+
+The WSI measured the vblank period once, right after configuring the 120 Hz
+mode. The output changes mode after that, and a display that re-syncs gives
+slow vblanks for a while. PSSwanStation on 120 Hz came up at 59.94 Hz at some
+starts and at 119.88 Hz at others. With VRR (attribute3 0x40000) it reported
+59.94 Hz while the display ran at 120: under VRR the display refreshes as
+flips come, and there was none yet.
+
+PS5_Mesa 08ba193, on 47e9eb6:
+
+- measures the period again for up to 1.5 s, until it is 120 Hz's;
+- still never counts a failed wait;
+- keeps 119.88 Hz for a title that declares VRR, even with slow vblanks
+  before its first flip.
+
+Console: PSSwanStation build 20 on the tester's PS5 with the same change on
+b3588f7. It came up at 119.88 Hz at every start, and with VRR reported
+119.88 Hz.
+
 ## 2026-10-12 — fragment shader barycentrics, in order
 
 `VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric` is reported again, now put in order by the compiler instead of by hardware that does
@@ -1043,3 +1063,10 @@ not do it. Mesa fork 1ba9874f478 (`radv/ps5: per-vertex fragment inputs in the p
 4. The smoke title's survey is now a set of checks (triangle list, strip, fan, lines in both provoking modes, `gl_BaryCoord`).
    The full smoke on this archive: 127 passed, 1 failed (display: its modes, which counts 2 modes since the console's
    resolution is 1440p, the 2026-10-10 entry).
+
+## 2026-10-18 — the 120 Hz settling and timed waits on the barycentrics pin (PS5 Mesa 14c2f44)
+
+PS5_Mesa 0ffa07e and 14c2f44 are 08ba193 (the 120 Hz mode measured until it
+settles, kept under VRR) and 5e99244 (timed waits on the clock the condition
+variable keeps, from Crux2) put on 1ba9874f478 unchanged; the pin moves to
+14c2f449851. Not yet run on the console.
